{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Contend</b> — The prophet rebukes the exiles, perhaps they will return and HaShem will restore their captivity, or he rebukes those generations before their exile." "<b>Her harlotries</b> — Doubled ayin, like בִּינָה הֲגִיגִי." "<b>And her adulteries</b> — Doubled lamed, like סַגְרִיר."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The lemma reads ונאפופיה with doubled lamed; Ibn Ezra's grammatical note derives this from the root לאף/נאף, explaining the lamed doubling by analogy with סגריר."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:49.608732855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}